<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The nemobot builder bot: builds one SCXML machine (never Rust) from a
  natural-language specification. Run it directly with scx run, giving it
  an env file and the builder.request on standard input (README.md,
  "Running"), or invoke it as a child and send it the request:

    <invoke id="builder" type="scxml" src="builder.scx"/>
    <send event="builder.request" target="#_builder"><content expr="..."/></send>

  It ends in exactly one of two top-level final states, whose <donedata>
  carries the result: done {scxml, schemas, tests, report} or failed
  {reason, diagnostics}. Run directly, scx run prints that data in its done
  record; invoked, the parent receives it as done.invoke.<id> (SCXML 6.4).
  Progress goes to <log>, labelled with the stage. The event:schema
  contracts below are inline copies of schemas/*.json (an invoked child is
  compiled at run time and gets no schema files); the builder_bot test
  (tests/tests/builder_bot.rs) keeps them equal.
  The events of the generate and decision services (generate.result,
  generate.failed, decision.abstain, decision.failed) are described here
  too, on the transitions that take them: a service package declares no
  event contract.

  intake -> design (an invoked generate service: topology plan) -> author
  (an invoked generate service: draft SCXML + event schemas + test scripts)
  -> validate (scx:validate with the draft profile; machine-applicable
  fixes through apply_fixes, at most 2 passes per draft) -> simulate (each
  test script drives the draft as an invoked child with its own invoke id)
  -> done. Every failure goes through retry_gate, which counts it
  and gives up after max_attempts; triage then reads its enabled
  event:schema transitions with decision:menu and invokes the decision
  service to pick one (repair while there is a plan, redesign, abandon).
  When the decision is unavailable (no key granted, backend failure:
  decision.failed or error.*), times out, or abstains, fallback decides by
  cond: redesign when there is no plan yet, else repair.

  Model calls are invoked services, never executable content: each runs
  while the session keeps processing events, its <finalize> records the
  result event, and done.invoke moves on. Bounds on time live in the
  topology: design and author arm builder.timeout after
  generate_timeout_ms and triage after decision_timeout_ms (each tagged with
  its stage run and cancelled on exit), and a timeout that fires first
  leaves the state, which cancels the in-flight call (its late answer
  reaches no one). The simulation is bounded the same way: each test runs
  at most sim_test_cap_ms, and simulate-timeout fires only after
  max_tests * sim_test_cap_ms plus a margin.

  The draft profile: drafts are model-written and run as invoked children
  of this session, which would inherit every namespace package and env
  value the run binds. validate therefore runs scx:validate with
  profile="draft", the validator's draft profile (scxml.rs
  docs/validator-rules.md, "Draft profile"): a draft that declares or uses a
  namespace other than SCXML and event (SCXML097), holds an invoke or script
  element (SCXML098), a src or srcexpr attribute (SCXML099), a typeexpr or a
  send type other than the SCXML Event I/O Processor (SCXML100), or a
  document type declaration (SCXML101) is an invalid draft, and its
  diagnostics go back to author like any other. The checks read the parsed
  XML (expanded names, so no prefix hides an element), never the text.

  Bindings: the scx namespace (built into scx), and the decision namespace
  package and the generate and decision service packages, resolved from their
  repository URIs; the env
  attributes below scope OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_BASE_URL to the generate
  service's invokes and TYPESAFE_API_KEY and TYPESAFE_BASE_URL to the
  decision service's.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:scx="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/scx"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/nemobot/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:env="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="builder" initial="intake">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The request. -->
    <data id="spec" expr="''"/>
    <data id="constraints" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="max_attempts" expr="3"/>
    <data id="model" expr="'gpt-6-luna'"/>
    <data id="generate_timeout_ms" expr="300000"/>
    <data id="decision_timeout_ms" expr="60000"/>
    <!-- The work. -->
    <data id="plan" expr="null"/>
    <data id="previous_plan" expr="null"/>
    <data id="draft" expr="null"/>
    <data id="previous_tests" expr="null"/>
    <data id="scxml_text" expr="null"/>
    <data id="parsed_schemas" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="report" expr="null"/>
    <data id="fixed" expr="null"/>
    <data id="mode" expr="'author'"/>
    <data id="schema_errors" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Model calls: the invocation in flight, its failure code, and the
         stage run its builder.timeout carries. -->
    <data id="gen_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
    <data id="decision_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="menu" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="stage_run" expr="0"/>
    <data id="design_system" expr="'You are the design stage of the nemobot builder bot. Plan the topology of one SCXML 1.0 state machine that implements the specification and honours every constraint. Use concise lowercase state ids (letters, digits, underscores). Name events with dotted lowercase names. Inputs are events the machine receives from its invoker; outputs are events it sends to its invoker. Model timing with delayed timer events, never with loops. When diagnostics or a previous plan are given, the previous attempt failed: plan again so that it cannot fail the same way. Answer with the plan only.'"/>
    <data id="author_system" expr="'You are the author stage of the nemobot builder bot. Write one complete SCXML 1.0 document that implements the plan and the specification. Rules: the root element is scxml in the namespace http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml with version 1.0 and datamodel ecmascript; use only core SCXML elements, plus the schema attribute of the namespace https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event (bound to the prefix event) to give each input event an inline JSON Schema on the transitions that take it, written as single-quoted JSON; no other namespaces, no src or srcexpr attributes, no script elements, no invoke elements, no type or typeexpr attribute on send (drafts that break these rules are refused before validation counts); every transition target names an existing state id; event descriptors are separated by spaces, never commas; send every output to the invoker with a send element whose target is #_parent, exactly once per occurrence (announce a state from its own onentry, not also from the transitions into it); the machine starts on its own in its initial state unless the specification names a start event; every state is reachable; implement timing with delayed sends (for example delay 3s) and cancel pending timers on exit. Also return schemas: one entry per input event, its schema as the JSON text of a JSON Schema object (for example {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;object&quot;}) equal to the inline one; and tests: one to eight test scripts, each with input events (name, data as JSON object text or the empty string, delay_ms from the start of the test), settle_ms (the total observation time from the start of the test, larger than every delay_ms), expect_events (the output event names the machine must send to #_parent, in order; other outputs may appear between them), and expect_done (whether the machine reaches a top-level final state within settle_ms; a machine that cycles forever never does). When the task is repair, previous_scxml and previous_tests failed with the given diagnostics: a simulate diagnostic means either the machine or the test expectation is wrong, so fix whichever disagrees with the specification, fix every other diagnostic, and keep what already works.'"/>
    <data id="triage_instructions" expr="'An SCXML draft failed. Choose how the builder continues: repair the draft from its diagnostics when they are local mistakes, redesign the plan when the diagnostics show the topology is wrong or there is no plan, abandon only when the specification cannot be built as a state machine.'"/>
    <data id="plan_schema" expr='({"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"summary":{"type":"string"},"states":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["atomic","compound","parallel","final"]},"parent":{"type":"string"},"purpose":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","kind","parent","purpose"],"additionalProperties":false}},"events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"direction":{"type":"string","enum":["input","output","internal"]},"description":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name","direction","description"],"additionalProperties":false}},"transitions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"source":{"type":"string"},"event":{"type":"string"},"target":{"type":"string"},"description":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","event","target","description"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["name","summary","states","events","transitions"],"additionalProperties":false})'/>
    <data id="draft_schema" expr='({"type":"object","properties":{"scxml":{"type":"string"},"schemas":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"event":{"type":"string"},"schema":{"type":"string"}},"required":["event","schema"],"additionalProperties":false}},"tests":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"data":{"type":"string"},"delay_ms":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["name","data","delay_ms"],"additionalProperties":false}},"settle_ms":{"type":"integer"},"expect_events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"expect_done":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["name","events","settle_ms","expect_events","expect_done"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["scxml","schemas","tests"],"additionalProperties":false})'/>
    <!-- Counters (every loop is bounded by one of them). -->
    <data id="attempt" expr="0"/>
    <data id="failures" expr="0"/>
    <data id="fix_passes" expr="0"/>
    <data id="fixes_applied" expr="0"/>
    <data id="warnings" expr="0"/>
    <!-- What went wrong last, and what was decided. -->
    <data id="diagnostics" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="decisions" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="attempt_log" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="failure_reason" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Simulation. -->
    <data id="max_tests" expr="8"/>
    <data id="sim_test_cap_ms" expr="120000"/>
    <data id="candidate_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="sim_index" expr="0"/>
    <!-- Counters of simulations and test runs: each control event the
         builder sends itself carries the one it belongs to, so a control
         event left on the queue by an earlier run never counts. -->
    <data id="simulation" expr="0"/>
    <data id="sim_run_seq" expr="0"/>
    <data id="sim_results" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="observed" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="child_done" expr="false"/>
    <data id="sim_error" expr="null"/>
    <data id="sim_sends" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="sent_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="step" expr="null"/>
    <data id="sid" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>

  <!-- Waits for builder.request; no timeout: the invoker owns the lifetime. -->
  <state id="intake">
    <transition event="builder.request" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"builder.request","description":"Ask the builder bot to build one SCXML machine from a natural-language specification.","type":"object","properties":{"spec":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"constraints":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":32},"max_attempts":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":8},"model":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"generate_timeout_ms":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":3600000}},"required":["spec"],"additionalProperties":false}'
                cond="_event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; !Array.isArray(_event.data) &amp;&amp; Object.keys(_event.data).every(function (k) { return ['spec', 'constraints', 'max_attempts', 'model', 'generate_timeout_ms'].indexOf(k) &gt;= 0; }) &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data.spec === 'string' &amp;&amp; _event.data.spec.trim().length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; (_event.data.constraints === undefined || (Array.isArray(_event.data.constraints) &amp;&amp; _event.data.constraints.length &lt;= 32 &amp;&amp; _event.data.constraints.every(function (c) { return typeof c === 'string'; }))) &amp;&amp; (_event.data.max_attempts === undefined || (Number.isInteger(_event.data.max_attempts) &amp;&amp; _event.data.max_attempts &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; _event.data.max_attempts &lt;= 8)) &amp;&amp; (_event.data.model === undefined || (typeof _event.data.model === 'string' &amp;&amp; _event.data.model.length &gt; 0)) &amp;&amp; (_event.data.generate_timeout_ms === undefined || (Number.isInteger(_event.data.generate_timeout_ms) &amp;&amp; _event.data.generate_timeout_ms &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; _event.data.generate_timeout_ms &lt;= 3600000))"
                target="design">
      <assign location="spec" expr="_event.data.spec"/>
      <assign location="constraints" expr="_event.data.constraints === undefined ? [] : _event.data.constraints"/>
      <assign location="max_attempts" expr="_event.data.max_attempts === undefined ? 3 : _event.data.max_attempts"/>
      <assign location="model" expr="_event.data.model === undefined ? 'gpt-6-luna' : _event.data.model"/>
      <assign location="generate_timeout_ms" expr="_event.data.generate_timeout_ms === undefined ? generate_timeout_ms : _event.data.generate_timeout_ms"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="builder.request" target="failed">
      <assign location="failure_reason" expr="'invalid-request'"/>
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'request', code: 'invalid-request', message: 'the builder.request data does not satisfy schemas/builder.request.json'}]"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- Plans the topology (structured output) through the generate service. -->
  <state id="design">
    <onentry>
      <!-- A failed redesign leaves plan null: keep the plan it replaces. -->
      <assign location="previous_plan" expr="plan !== null ? plan : previous_plan"/>
      <assign location="plan" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="stage_run" expr="stage_run + 1"/>
      <log label="design" expr="(previous_plan === null ? 'planning' : 'replanning') + ' the topology; failures ' + failures + ' of ' + max_attempts"/>
      <send id="design-timeout" event="builder.timeout" delayexpr="generate_timeout_ms + 'ms'">
        <param name="run" expr="stage_run"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendid="design-timeout"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke idlocation="gen_id" type="https://github.com/stateforward/nemobot/services/generate"
            env:apikey="OPENAI_API_KEY" env:baseurl="OPENAI_BASE_URL">
      <param name="model" expr="model"/>
      <param name="system" expr="design_system"/>
      <param name="prompt" expr="JSON.stringify({task: 'design', spec: spec, constraints: constraints, previous_plan: previous_plan, diagnostics: diagnostics})"/>
      <param name="schema" expr="plan_schema"/>
      <param name="schemaname" expr="'topology_plan'"/>
      <param name="strict" expr="true"/>
      <finalize>
        <assign location="plan" expr="_event.name === 'generate.result' ? _event.data.json : plan"/>
        <assign location="gen_failure" expr="_event.name === 'generate.failed' ? _event.data.code : gen_failure"/>
      </finalize>
    </invoke>
    <!-- The two events of the generate service; <finalize> records them. -->
    <transition event="generate.result" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"generate.result","description":"The reply of the generate service: text without a requested schema, or the JSON value that satisfies the requested schema.","oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"}},"required":["text"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"json":true},"required":["json"],"additionalProperties":false}]}'/>
    <transition event="generate.failed" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"generate.failed","description":"The generation failed; code names why (closed).","type":"object","properties":{"code":{"enum":["unconfigured","transport","status","malformed","truncated","filtered","refusal","not-json","schema-mismatch"]}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":false}'/>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="_event.invokeid === gen_id &amp;&amp; plan !== null" target="author">
      <assign location="mode" expr="'author'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="_event.invokeid === gen_id" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'generate', code: 'design-failed', message: 'the design generation failed (' + gen_failure + '): no plan within the plan schema'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Only this stage run's own timeout; it preempts the call in flight
         (leaving design cancels the invocation). -->
    <transition event="builder.timeout" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; _event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === stage_run" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'timeout', code: 'design-timeout', message: 'the design generation did not answer within ' + generate_timeout_ms + ' ms and was cancelled'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.execution" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'generate', code: 'design-failed', message: 'the design generation could not start'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.communication" cond="_event.invokeid === gen_id" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'generate', code: 'design-failed', message: 'the design generation failed'}]"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- Writes the draft: SCXML, its input event schemas, and test scripts. -->
  <state id="author">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="attempt" expr="attempt + 1"/>
      <log label="author" expr="mode + ' draft, attempt ' + attempt"/>
      <assign location="previous_tests" expr="draft === null ? null : draft.tests"/>
      <assign location="draft" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="stage_run" expr="stage_run + 1"/>
      <send id="author-timeout" event="builder.timeout" delayexpr="generate_timeout_ms + 'ms'">
        <param name="run" expr="stage_run"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendid="author-timeout"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke idlocation="gen_id" type="https://github.com/stateforward/nemobot/services/generate"
            env:apikey="OPENAI_API_KEY" env:baseurl="OPENAI_BASE_URL">
      <param name="model" expr="model"/>
      <param name="system" expr="author_system"/>
      <param name="prompt" expr="JSON.stringify({task: mode, spec: spec, constraints: constraints, plan: plan, previous_scxml: mode === 'repair' ? scxml_text : null, previous_tests: mode === 'repair' ? previous_tests : null, diagnostics: diagnostics})"/>
      <param name="schema" expr="draft_schema"/>
      <param name="schemaname" expr="'scxml_draft'"/>
      <param name="strict" expr="true"/>
      <finalize>
        <assign location="draft" expr="_event.name === 'generate.result' ? _event.data.json : draft"/>
        <assign location="gen_failure" expr="_event.name === 'generate.failed' ? _event.data.code : gen_failure"/>
      </finalize>
    </invoke>
    <!-- The two events of the generate service; <finalize> records them. -->
    <transition event="generate.result" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"generate.result","description":"The reply of the generate service: text without a requested schema, or the JSON value that satisfies the requested schema.","oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"}},"required":["text"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"json":true},"required":["json"],"additionalProperties":false}]}'/>
    <transition event="generate.failed" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"generate.failed","description":"The generation failed; code names why (closed).","type":"object","properties":{"code":{"enum":["unconfigured","transport","status","malformed","truncated","filtered","refusal","not-json","schema-mismatch"]}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":false}'/>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="_event.invokeid === gen_id &amp;&amp; draft !== null" target="validate">
      <assign location="scxml_text" expr="draft.scxml"/>
      <assign location="fix_passes" expr="0"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="_event.invokeid === gen_id" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'generate', code: 'author-failed', message: 'the author generation failed (' + gen_failure + '): no draft within the draft schema'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="builder.timeout" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; _event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === stage_run" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'timeout', code: 'author-timeout', message: 'the author generation did not answer within ' + generate_timeout_ms + ' ms and was cancelled'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.execution" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'generate', code: 'author-failed', message: 'the author generation could not start'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.communication" cond="_event.invokeid === gen_id" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'generate', code: 'author-failed', message: 'the author generation failed'}]"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- Checks the draft: its schemas parse, the validator is clean, its test
       scripts are within bounds. -->
  <state id="validate">
    <onentry>
      <log label="validate" expr="'validating the draft'"/>
      <assign location="report" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="fixed" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="schema_errors" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="parsed_schemas" expr="draft.schemas.map(function (s) { var value = null; try { value = JSON.parse(s.schema); } catch (e) { value = null; } if (value === null || (typeof value !== 'object' &amp;&amp; typeof value !== 'boolean') || Array.isArray(value)) { schema_errors.push({kind: 'draft', code: 'schema-not-json', message: 'the schemas entry of ' + JSON.stringify(s.event) + ' is not a JSON Schema object as JSON text: ' + JSON.stringify(String(s.schema).slice(0, 200))}); } return {event: s.event, schema: value}; })"/>
      <scx:validate location="report" expr="scxml_text" name="draft.scx" profile="draft"
                   applyfixes="machine-applicable" fixedlocation="fixed"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition cond="report !== null &amp;&amp; schema_errors.length &gt; 0" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="schema_errors.slice(0, 20)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="report !== null &amp;&amp; report.validator.counts.errors === 0 &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(draft.tests) &amp;&amp; draft.tests.length &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; draft.tests.length &lt;= max_tests &amp;&amp; draft.tests.every(function (t) { return t.events.length &lt;= 32; })"
                target="simulate">
      <assign location="warnings" expr="report.validator.counts.warnings"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="report !== null &amp;&amp; report.validator.counts.errors === 0" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'draft', code: 'tests-out-of-bounds', message: 'the draft must carry one to eight test scripts of at most 32 events each'}]"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="report !== null &amp;&amp; typeof fixed === 'string' &amp;&amp; fixed !== scxml_text &amp;&amp; fix_passes &lt; 2"
                target="apply_fixes"/>
    <transition cond="report !== null" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="report.validator.diagnostics.filter(function (d) { return d.severity === 'error'; }).slice(0, 20).map(function (d) { return {kind: 'validate', code: d.code, message: d.help ? d.message + ' Help: ' + d.help : d.message}; })"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.execution" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'draft', code: 'validator-failed', message: 'the validator could not check the draft (an oversized or unreadable document)'}]"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- Takes the validator's machine-applicable fixes, then validates again. -->
  <state id="apply_fixes">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="scxml_text" expr="fixed"/>
      <assign location="fix_passes" expr="fix_passes + 1"/>
      <assign location="fixes_applied" expr="fixes_applied + 1"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition target="validate"/>
  </state>

  <!-- Runs every test script against the draft as an invoked child. The
       timeout covers the longest simulation validate admits (max_tests
       tests of at most sim_test_cap_ms each) plus a margin. -->
  <state id="simulate" initial="sim_next">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="simulation" expr="simulation + 1"/>
      <log label="simulate" expr="draft.tests.length + ' test script(s)'"/>
      <send id="simulate-timeout" event="builder.timeout" delayexpr="(max_tests * sim_test_cap_ms + 60000) + 'ms'">
        <param name="run" expr="simulation"/>
      </send>
      <assign location="sim_index" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="sim_results" expr="[]"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendid="simulate-timeout"/>
    </onexit>
    <!-- Only this simulation's own timeout: a candidate's event of that name
         (it carries an invoke id, also after its invocation was cancelled)
         and an earlier simulation's fired timeout fall through. -->
    <transition event="builder.timeout" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; _event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === simulation" target="retry_gate">
      <assign location="diagnostics" expr="[{kind: 'timeout', code: 'simulate-timeout', message: 'the simulation did not finish in time'}]"/>
    </transition>

    <state id="sim_next">
      <transition cond="sim_index &gt;= draft.tests.length" target="sim_verdict"/>
      <transition target="sim_run"/>
    </state>

    <!-- One test: the draft runs as a fresh invocation (its own generated
         id in candidate_id, so nothing a cancelled earlier candidate left
         on the queue counts) for the script's settle time. -->
    <state id="sim_run">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="observed" expr="[]"/>
        <assign location="child_done" expr="false"/>
        <assign location="sim_error" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="sim_sends" expr="[]"/>
        <assign location="sim_run_seq" expr="sim_run_seq + 1"/>
        <!-- Processed after the invocation starts (external queue). A run
             whose invocation fails to start ends on error.execution before
             this is processed; the tag keeps the next run from taking it. -->
        <send event="sim.drive">
          <param name="run" expr="sim_run_seq"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <foreach array="sim_sends" item="sid">
          <cancel sendidexpr="sid"/>
        </foreach>
        <cancel sendid="sim-settle"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke idlocation="candidate_id" type="scxml">
        <content expr="scxml_text"/>
      </invoke>
      <!-- The builder's own control events never carry an invoke id and
           carry this run's tag; a candidate's events of the same names fall
           through to the recorder below, and an earlier run's are dropped. -->
      <transition event="sim.drive" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; _event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === sim_run_seq">
        <foreach array="draft.tests[sim_index].events" item="step">
          <send eventexpr="step.name" targetexpr="'#_' + candidate_id" idlocation="sent_id"
                delayexpr="Math.min(Math.max(step.delay_ms, 0), 60000) + 'ms'">
            <content expr="step.data === '' ? null : JSON.parse(step.data)"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="sim_sends" expr="sim_sends.concat([sent_id])"/>
        </foreach>
        <send id="sim-settle" event="sim.settle"
              delayexpr="Math.min(sim_test_cap_ms, Math.max.apply(null, [1, draft.tests[sim_index].settle_ms].concat(draft.tests[sim_index].events.map(function (e) { return e.delay_ms + 1; })))) + 'ms'">
          <param name="run" expr="sim_run_seq"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke" cond="_event.invokeid === candidate_id" target="sim_check">
        <assign location="child_done" expr="true"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="sim.settle" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; _event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === sim_run_seq" target="sim_check"/>
      <transition event="error.*" cond="!_event.invokeid || _event.invokeid === candidate_id" target="sim_check">
        <assign location="sim_error" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="*" cond="_event.invokeid === candidate_id">
        <assign location="observed" expr="observed.concat([_event.name])"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- Compares one test's outputs with its expectations: expect_events in
         order (other outputs may come between), and expect_done. -->
    <state id="sim_check">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="sim_results" expr="sim_results.concat([(function (t) { var next = 0; observed.forEach(function (name) { if (next &lt; t.expect_events.length &amp;&amp; name === t.expect_events[next]) { next += 1; } }); return {name: t.name, invokeid: candidate_id, passed: sim_error === null &amp;&amp; next === t.expect_events.length &amp;&amp; child_done === t.expect_done, observed: observed, expected: t.expect_events, done: child_done, expect_done: t.expect_done, error: sim_error}; })(draft.tests[sim_index])])"/>
        <assign location="sim_index" expr="sim_index + 1"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="sim_next"/>
    </state>

    <state id="sim_verdict">
      <transition cond="sim_results.every(function (r) { return r.passed; })" target="done"/>
      <transition target="retry_gate">
        <assign location="diagnostics" expr="sim_results.filter(function (r) { return !r.passed; }).map(function (r) { return {kind: 'simulate', code: 'test-failed', message: 'test ' + r.name + ' expected the outputs ' + JSON.stringify(r.expected) + ' in order and done=' + r.expect_done + ', observed ' + JSON.stringify(r.observed) + ' and done=' + r.done + (r.error === null ? '' : ', error ' + r.error)}; })"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- Counts one failure; gives up after max_attempts. -->
  <state id="retry_gate">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="failures" expr="failures + 1"/>
      <assign location="attempt_log" expr="attempt_log.concat([{failure: failures, attempt: attempt, diagnostics: diagnostics.slice(0, 5)}])"/>
      <log label="retry_gate" expr="'failure ' + failures + ' of ' + max_attempts + (diagnostics.length &gt; 0 ? ': ' + diagnostics[0].kind + ' ' + diagnostics[0].code : '')"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition cond="failures &gt;= max_attempts" target="failed">
      <assign location="failure_reason" expr="'attempts-exhausted'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition target="triage"/>
  </state>

  <!-- Picks the next step among the enabled event:schema transitions:
       decision:menu reads them (synchronously), and the decision service
       chooses one and emits it. -->
  <state id="triage">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="stage_run" expr="stage_run + 1"/>
      <decision:menu location="menu"/>
      <log label="triage" expr="'choosing among ' + menu.length + ' option(s)'"/>
      <send id="triage-timeout" event="builder.timeout" delayexpr="decision_timeout_ms + 'ms'">
        <param name="run" expr="stage_run"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendid="triage-timeout"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke idlocation="decision_id" type="https://github.com/stateforward/nemobot/services/decision"
            env:apikey="TYPESAFE_API_KEY" env:baseurl="TYPESAFE_BASE_URL">
      <param name="menu" expr="menu"/>
      <param name="state" expr="({spec: spec, attempt: attempt, failures: failures, max_attempts: max_attempts, has_plan: plan !== null, diagnostics: diagnostics})"/>
      <param name="instructions" expr="triage_instructions"/>
    </invoke>
    <transition event="triage.repair" cond="plan !== null" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"triage.repair","description":"Repair the current draft: author it again from the same plan with the diagnostics of the failed attempt.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false}' target="author">
      <assign location="mode" expr="'repair'"/>
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['triage.repair'])"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Repair needs a plan (the done data reports it); without one, a
         triage.repair (never offered then) redesigns. -->
    <transition event="triage.repair" target="design">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['triage.repair'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="triage.redesign" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"triage.redesign","description":"Redesign: plan the topology again, then author a new draft, because the plan itself looks wrong.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false}' target="design">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['triage.redesign'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="triage.abandon" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"triage.abandon","description":"Give up: the specification cannot be built as an SCXML machine, so end in the final state failed.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false}' target="failed">
      <assign location="failure_reason" expr="'abandoned'"/>
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['triage.abandon'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.abstain" cond="decision_id !== null &amp;&amp; _event.invokeid === decision_id" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"decision.abstain","description":"The decision service took no event: nothing was offered, the backend declined, or the probability of the chosen event was below the threshold.","type":"object","properties":{"reason":{"enum":["no-candidates","declined","below-threshold"]},"confidence":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}},"required":["reason"],"additionalProperties":false}' target="fallback">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['fallback:abstain'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.failed" cond="decision_id !== null &amp;&amp; _event.invokeid === decision_id" event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"decision.failed","description":"The decision failed; code names why (closed).","type":"object","properties":{"code":{"enum":["unconfigured","transport","status","malformed","schema-mismatch"]}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":false}' target="fallback">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['fallback:unavailable'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="builder.timeout" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; _event.data !== null &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data === 'object' &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === stage_run" target="fallback">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['fallback:timeout'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.execution" target="fallback">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['fallback:unavailable'])"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.communication" cond="_event.invokeid === decision_id" target="fallback">
      <assign location="decisions" expr="decisions.concat(['fallback:unavailable'])"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The cond-based decision when the decision service is unavailable,
       times out, or abstains: redesign without a plan, else repair. -->
  <state id="fallback">
    <transition cond="plan === null" target="design"/>
    <transition target="author">
      <assign location="mode" expr="'repair'"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The two outcomes. Run directly, scx run prints the donedata in its
       done record; invoked, the parent gets it as done.invoke.<id>. -->
  <final id="done">
    <onentry>
      <log label="done" expr="'built ' + (plan === null ? 'a machine' : plan.name) + ' in ' + attempt + ' attempt(s)'"/>
    </onentry>
    <donedata event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"done","description":"The donedata of the final state done of the builder bot: an SCXML machine that validates and passes its own simulation.","type":"object","properties":{"scxml":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"schemas":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"event":{"type":"string"},"schema":{"type":["object","boolean"]}},"required":["event","schema"],"additionalProperties":false}},"tests":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"report":{"type":"object","properties":{"attempts":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"failures":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"fixes_applied":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"warnings":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"plan":{"type":"object"},"decisions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"history":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"simulation":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}}},"required":["attempts","failures","fixes_applied","warnings","plan","decisions","history","simulation"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["scxml","schemas","tests","report"],"additionalProperties":false}'>
      <content expr="({scxml: scxml_text, schemas: parsed_schemas, tests: draft.tests, report: {attempts: attempt, failures: failures, fixes_applied: fixes_applied, warnings: warnings, plan: plan, decisions: decisions, history: attempt_log, simulation: sim_results}})"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>

  <final id="failed">
    <onentry>
      <log label="failed" expr="failure_reason"/>
    </onentry>
    <donedata event:schema='{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"failed","description":"The donedata of the final state failed of the builder bot: why it could not build a machine that validates and passes its simulation.","type":"object","properties":{"reason":{"enum":["invalid-request","attempts-exhausted","abandoned"]},"diagnostics":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"enum":["request","generate","draft","validate","simulate","timeout"]},"code":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind","code","message"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["reason","diagnostics"],"additionalProperties":false}'>
      <content expr="({reason: failure_reason, diagnostics: diagnostics.map(function (d) { return {kind: d.kind, code: d.code, message: d.message}; })})"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
